# CodeRabbit + merge loops (`dev` → `main`)

Use this with **pull-requests.mdc** whenever the user runs `/loop`, autopilot, or “until merge” on the open **`dev` → `main`** PR.

## Merge authority

**Merge without asking** when the user:

- Says merge if ready / don’t wait for confirmation / loop until merge / autopilot until merged, or
- Includes merge intent in the `/loop` prompt.

**Do not merge** only when the user **explicitly** forbids it in the same thread (e.g. “do not merge”, “review only”).

When merge-ready (below), run `gh pr merge <number> --merge` in the **same pass**. Do not report “ready for merge” and arm another long sleep if nothing is left to fix.

## Merge-ready checklist (all required)

1. PR is **OPEN**, **MERGEABLE**, merge state **CLEAN** (or equivalent).
2. Required CI **success**: at minimum **`rust`** and **`native-and-ts`** on the current PR head.
3. **CodeRabbit** not `pending` / `in progress` / `queued` on the current head.
4. **No actionable CodeRabbit findings** left after full triage (inline **and** outside-diff — see below).
5. **All** GitHub **review threads resolved** (you may resolve them after verifying the fix).

If (1)–(4) hold but (5) has stale open threads for code already fixed: **resolve those threads**, then merge.

If you push fixes: re-run the checklist on the **new** head (wait for CI + CodeRabbit idle before merge).

## CodeRabbit triage — every loop wake (mandatory)

**Inline-only triage is incomplete.** CodeRabbit often puts findings only in the **review summary** under **Outside diff range comments** (GitHub cannot attach them to the diff). Those never show up as unresolved inline threads.

### A. Refresh PR head and checks

```bash
gh pr view <n> --json number,headRefOid,mergeable,mergeStateStatus,state,statusCheckRollup
gh pr checks <n>
```

### B. Unresolved review threads (GraphQL)

```graphql
query { repository(owner:"OWNER", name:"REPO") { pullRequest(number:N) {
  reviewThreads(first:100) { nodes { id isResolved path line
    comments(last:1) { nodes { body author { login } } } } } } } }
```

Fix or dismiss each unresolved thread; then resolve via:

```graphql
mutation { resolveReviewThread(input: {threadId: "PRRT_..."}) { thread { isResolved } } }
```

### C. Pull request inline comments

```bash
gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/N/comments
```

Include comments on **older commits** if the finding still applies to current code. Ignore bodies that say **Addressed in commit …** only after you **verify** on HEAD.

### D. CodeRabbit review bodies (outside diff + summary)

```bash
gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/N/reviews \
  --jq '.[] | select(.user.login|test("coderabbit";"i")) | {id, commit_id, submitted_at, body}'
```

For **each** CodeRabbit review (prioritize reviews whose `commit_id` matches PR head, then the newest):

1. If the body contains **`Outside diff range comments`** or **outside the diff**, read **every** nested block (usually `<details><summary>… · <code>path:line</code>`). Extract path and line range; implement valid fixes on `dev`.
2. Note **`Actionable comments posted: N`**. If N > 0, ensure all N are accounted for (inline + outside-diff), not only open threads.
3. Treat **Minor**, **Quick win**, and **Major** the same for implementation: if the finding is still valid, fix it. Do not skip “minor” items to save time.

Example review URL pattern: `pullrequestreview-<id>` → fetch with:

```bash
gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/N/reviews/<review_id> --jq .body
```

### E. Fix, test, changelog

- Smallest correct diff on **`dev`**; run scoped tests.
- Update root **CHANGELOG.md** `[Unreleased]` for user-facing package/crate changes.
- Commit, push **`dev`**; **`gh pr edit`** if PR scope/title/body needs refresh.

### F. Resolve threads proactively

CodeRabbit **does not** always mark threads resolved. After you fix or confirm existing code matches the suggestion:

- Resolve the GitHub review thread (mutation above).
- Optionally reply briefly: fixed in `<short-sha>`.

Do not leave threads open “for CodeRabbit” if you are confident the comment is satisfied.

### G. Merge or re-wait (same pass)

| State | Action |
|--------|--------|
| User granted merge + checklist pass on current head | **`gh pr merge N --merge`**; stop loop timers |
| Fixes just pushed | Watch CI (`gh run watch …`); short heartbeat; repeat A–G on new head |
| CodeRabbit still running | Short heartbeat only; **do not** treat as merge-ready |
| CI green + CodeRabbit idle + no actionable items + threads resolved | **Merge** (if merge authority); do not wait for user |

## Anti-patterns

- Polling for an hour after CI and CodeRabbit are already green with zero open findings.
- Triage only GraphQL unresolved threads and inline comments, **missing outside-diff** review text.
- Assuming “Review completed” means nothing left to do without parsing the latest review body.
- Skipping **Minor** / **Quick win** comments.
- Waiting for the user to say “merge” when the loop already authorized it.
